67,3,2,talk,Minato,,"I think accuracy is a form of respect. If I use more, I should pay more. That is fair.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"The winter habits show that without a meter, people waste. Option A stops that waste.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,Option B means I have to do a big calculation once a year. That is a lot of stress at once.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,Option B is a middle path. It smooths out the spikes. It feels like a gentle rhythm.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Midori,,Option B still requires a year-end settlement. That is a moment of potential conflict. I prefer C.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minato,,Option B hides the monthly variance. I want to see the real cost as it happens.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"Option B is risky. If the winter is colder than expected, my share could double. I need A.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,Option A means I just read a number. I do not have to calculate anything. That is the best for me.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
